// THE DOCUMENT PAGES: /about (the repo README), /resources, /glossary,
// /constitution and /guides/data-views. Five pages, one stylesheet, and all of
// them are long-form reading rather than app chrome — which is exactly what
// app/styles/prose-form.styl is for, so they now speak that language instead of
// carrying their own near-copy of it.
//
// What that replaced, since each item is a thing not to reintroduce: private
// $markdown_sans / $markdown_mono tokens duplicating $prose_sans / $prose_mono;
// the app's mid-grey $textColor as body ink on a page read in paragraphs; links
// in pure `red` at weight 700, a weight this site does not load, so every link
// on every document rendered as a synthesized bold; and a three-layer Material
// elevation shadow under every table, which is the same fingerprint the menu
// buttons were taken off.
//
// The serif constitution below is the one part that stays its own thing, and
// its reason is at that rule.

// Legal documents read as serif; system faces only — no extra webfont payload.
$markdown_serif = 'Iowan Old Style', 'Palatino Linotype', Palatino, 'Book Antiqua', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif

// THESE PAGES DO NOT PAINT A SURFACE, deliberately. They take the app's
// $backgroundColor from body, which is the same surface the menu drawer
// carries — a document page briefly went to paper here and the drawer then sat
// as a grey panel against a white page, which reads as the menu being broken
// rather than as the page being paper. The landing and auth pages can afford
// paper because they are the site's front door; a document opened from the
// menu sits beside the menu.
.markdown
  prose_page()
  // prose_page() paints no background of its own, so body shows through.
  // prose_page() sets the 680px prose measure, which is right for a page of
  // pure text and too narrow for these: the glossary and the data-views guide
  // are mostly tables, and a table forced to 680px wraps every cell. The
  // authored two-column documents get the full width; everything else gets a
  // measure a little past prose, wide enough for a table and a code block.
  max-width 1300px

  &:not(:has(.table-of-contents))
    max-width 820px

  // The first block sits directly under the page chrome; its heading margin
  // would otherwise open a large gap above the title.
  > :first-child
  .body > :first-child
    margin-top 0

  // The global bare `p` rule in styles/general.styl pins font, leading and
  // tracking; take them back so a document can set its own type.
  p
    margin 0 0 1em
    font-family inherit
    line-height inherit
    letter-spacing normal

  // COMMA-SEPARATED ON ONE LINE, NOT A SELECTOR PER LINE. Stylus reads a
  // newline-separated group correctly only while each line is a SINGLE token:
  // give it two lines that each carry a descendant selector and it silently
  // emits the last one alone. `ul ul` / `ol ol` written on two lines compiled
  // to `.markdown ol ol` and nothing else, so nested bullet lists never got
  // these margins — a real defect in this file, not a hypothetical.
  ul
  ol
    margin 0 0 1em
    padding-left 1.5em
    ul, ol
      margin-top 0.5em
      margin-bottom 0.5em

  ul
    list-style-type disc

  ol
    list-style-type decimal

  li
    margin-bottom 0.4em

  // THE TABLE OF CONTENTS IS AN INDEX, NOT PROSE. It is authored in the
  // document itself (docs/glossary.md, docs/resources.md and the data-views
  // guide each open with a .table-of-contents div), so everything in it would
  // otherwise inherit the body treatment: bullet markers competing with the
  // link text, prose_page()'s mono-600-with-a-rule on every entry, and the
  // heading scale on its own label. At forty-odd entries that reads as a
  // second document stacked in front of the first.
  .table-of-contents
    // Its label is a label, not a heading — the same small tracked mono the
    // rest of the site uses to name a region.
    h1
    h2
    h3
    h4
    h5
    h6
      prose_section_title()
      margin 0 0 14px
      font-size 0.6875em

    ul
    ol
      list-style-type none
      margin 0
      padding-left 0

    li
      margin 0

    // marked wraps a list item that has children in a <p>, so a top-level
    // entry arrives as `<li><p><a>` while its children are bare `<li><a>`.
    // That paragraph carries the body's 1em bottom margin and opened a gap
    // under every parent entry.
    li > p
      margin 0

    // Depth is carried by a rule as well as by indent, so a nested entry is
    // placed at a glance in a list this long. Comma-separated for the reason
    // given on the nested-list rule above.
    ul ul, ol ol
      margin 4px 0 10px
      padding-left 14px
      border-left 1px solid $prose_rule_strong

    a
      display block
      padding 4px 0
      font-family $prose_sans
      font-weight 400
      font-size 0.8125em
      line-height 1.45
      border-bottom none
      color $prose_muted
      transition color 120ms ease
      &:hover
        color $prose_accent
      &:focus-visible
        outline 2px solid $prose_accent
        outline-offset 2px

    // The top level is the document's own sections and everything beneath it is
    // a subsection; without a weight difference a forty-entry index is one flat
    // list and the reader cannot see the document's shape in it.
    > ul > li > p > a, > ul > li > a
      color $prose_ink
      font-weight $prose_bold

  // Anchors outside the index inherit prose_page()'s treatment: ink, mono, 600,
  // a rule underneath, accent on hover. Nothing to restate here.

  h1
  h2
  h3
  h4
  h5
  h6
    font-family $prose_mono
    font-weight $prose_bold
    color $prose_ink
    line-height 1.25
    letter-spacing -0.01em
    margin 1.6em 0 0.5em

  h1
    font-size 2em
    margin-top 1em
    letter-spacing -0.02em
  h2
    font-size 1.5em
  h3
    font-size 1.25em
  h4
    font-size 1.0625em
  h5
    font-size 1em
  h6
    font-size 0.9375em
    color $prose_muted

  blockquote
    margin 0 0 1em
    padding 0.25em 0 0.25em 1.25em
    border-left 3px solid $prose_rule_strong
    color $prose_muted

  // A table is data, so it is ruled rather than boxed: hairlines and the paper
  // it already sits on, with no fill and no shadow. The elevation shadow that
  // used to be here was Material's three-layer one.
  table
    width 100%
    border-collapse collapse
    font-family $prose_sans
    font-size 0.9375em
    margin 0 0 1.5em

    code
      white-space nowrap

  th
    text-align start
    padding 8px 14px 8px 0
    border-bottom 1px solid $prose_rule_strong
    font-family $prose_mono
    font-weight $prose_bold
    font-size 0.8125em
    letter-spacing 0.06em
    text-transform uppercase
    color $prose_muted

  td
    padding 8px 14px 8px 0
    border-bottom 1px solid $prose_rule
    vertical-align top

  // Last column runs to the measure's edge rather than carrying trailing
  // padding that reads as a ragged right rule.
  th:last-child
  td:last-child
    padding-right 0

  pre
    background $prose_paper
    border 1px solid $prose_rule
    border-radius 3px
    padding 14px 16px
    margin 0 0 1.5em
    overflow-x auto
    white-space break-spaces
    font-family $prose_mono
    font-size 0.875em
    line-height 1.6
    color $prose_ink

  code:not(pre > code)
    font-family $prose_mono
    background $prose_paper
    border 1px solid $prose_rule
    border-radius 3px
    padding 1px 5px
    font-size 0.875em
    white-space nowrap

  hr
    border none
    border-top 1px solid $prose_rule
    margin 2.5em 0

  // Constitution — styled as a legal instrument: serif text, centered article
  // headings, and lettered subsections. The document references its own
  // subsections by letter ("Article III, Section 2, Subsection f"), so the
  // nested ordered lists must be lettered rather than numbered to match.
  //
  // This is the one document that does NOT take the prose faces, and the one
  // place 700 is still correct: $prose_bold is 600 because Inter and IBM Plex
  // Mono are loaded at 600 and not at 700, but the serif stack here is entirely
  // system faces, which carry a real 700. Asking for it costs no payload and
  // gets a drawn bold rather than a synthesized one.
  &.markdown__constitution
    max-width 800px
    font-family $markdown_serif
    font-size 17px
    line-height 1.75
    color $prose_ink

    p
    li
      text-align justify
      hyphens auto

    h1
    h2
    h3
    h4
    h5
    h6
      font-family $markdown_serif
      letter-spacing normal

    h1
      margin 0.5em 0 0.25em
      font-size 1.875em
      font-weight 700
      text-align center
      text-transform uppercase
      letter-spacing 0.08em
      line-height 1.3

    // "(Originally adopted 2020)" — the document's attestation line.
    h1 + p
      margin-bottom 2em
      text-align center
      font-style italic
      color $prose_muted
      border-bottom 4px double $prose_rule_strong
      padding-bottom 1.25em

    // "Article I"
    h2
      margin 2.25em 0 0.4em
      font-size 1.375em
      font-weight 700
      text-align center
      text-transform uppercase
      letter-spacing 0.16em

    // The article title, authored as a bold paragraph under each "Article N".
    h2 + p
      margin-bottom 1.75em
      text-align center
      text-transform uppercase
      letter-spacing 0.06em
      font-size 0.9375em
      strong
        font-weight 700

    // Section headings within an article.
    h3
      margin 2em 0 0.6em
      font-size 1.0625em
      font-weight 700
      font-style italic

    // Top-level items carry the section number the document cites.
    ol
      padding-left 2.25em
      > li::marker
        font-weight 700

    ol ol
      list-style-type lower-alpha
    ol ol ol
      list-style-type lower-roman

    blockquote
      margin 0 0 1em 1.5em
      padding-left 1.25em
      font-style italic

    // Schedules and the amendment history are tabular data, not prose.
    table
      font-family $prose_sans
      text-align left

    // The link rule reads as a foreign mark in a justified serif column, so it
    // carries the serif and marks itself with weight instead.
    a
      font-family $markdown_serif
      font-weight 700
      border-bottom none
      &:hover
        border-bottom 1px solid $prose_accent

// Below this width the index is a block at the head of the document rather
// than a column beside it, so it needs a foot rule to close it off — without
// one it runs straight into the first section and reads as the opening list.
@media (max-width: 959px)
  .markdown .table-of-contents
    margin 0 0 2.5em
    padding-bottom 1.5em
    border-bottom 1px solid $prose_rule

@media (min-width: 960px)
  .markdown:has(.table-of-contents)
    align-items flex-start
    flex-direction row-reverse
    display flex

    .table-of-contents
      position fixed
      // Clear of the app banner when one is showing, the same variable the nav
      // drawer anchors to, rather than a fixed inset that the banner overlaps.
      top var(--app-banner-height, 0px)
      bottom 0
      // `auto`, not `scroll`: a short index under `scroll` renders a dead
      // scrollbar gutter down the column for its whole height.
      overflow-y auto
      width 240px
      padding 88px 0 48px 24px
      border-left 1px solid $prose_rule

    .body
      margin-right 288px
